  "summary": "pgx server-side implementation panic on malformed input",
  "details": "[pgx](github.com/jackc/pgx/v5) is a pure Go driver and toolkit for PostgreSQL. pgx's server-side PostgreSQL protocol implementation prior to v5.9.0 contains an out-of-bound slice access that can be triggered with crafted packets and leads to panic and process termination.\n\nMost users use this library as PostgreSQL client, and thus are unaffected.",
